# List page pattern (entire app)

Applies to **every** index/list screen in the product — admin, agent, customer, or any future portal — not only `/admin`.

Examples: customers, projects, plots, bookings, payments, agents, notifications, and any new list.

Use this UI — not filter tab chips, not a Search button form, not a card grid.

## Toolbar

1. Primary action top-right only (`New …` / `Add …`) — no page title / subtitle on the list.
2. Use shared `ListSearchBar` from `@/components/ui` (wrap in `<Suspense fallback={<ListSearchBarFallback />}>`).
3. Search field: magnifying glass left, placeholder `Search {entity}`, rounded-xl, light border, white bg.
4. Matching square filter button (funnel icon) to the right — dropdown for status/filters. Empty `key: ""` = All (omit query param).
5. Multi-dimension filters: pass `filterGroups` instead of `filters`.
6. Pass the correct `basePath` for that route (e.g. `/admin/plots`, `/agent/bookings`).

```tsx
<Suspense fallback={<ListSearchBarFallback />}>
  <ListSearchBar
    basePath="/admin/plots"
    placeholder="Search plots"
    initialQ={q}
    filterGroups={groups}
  />
</Suspense>
```

## Results

- No outer `surface` / card wrapper around the whole list.
- Desktop: `data-table` with avatar/initials + status pill on the primary column.
- Mobile: simple row list (`px-3 py-2.5`).
- Empty: `EmptyState` with match vs empty-copy based on `q` / filter.

## No separator lines (any list)

**Never** put horizontal divider lines between list rows — anywhere in the app (index lists, dashboard lists, nested plot lists, detail field rows that act like lists).

- ❌ `divide-y`, `divide-border`, per-row `border-b` / `border-t`
- ❌ `data-table` body row borders (`.data-table td` must stay borderless)
- ✅ Separate rows with padding only (`py-2.5` / table cell padding)
- ✅ A single header underline under `thead` / section title is OK; not between items

## Do not

- ❌ `AdminFilterTabs` / segmented filter chips on list pages
- ❌ `surface` + text “Search” button
- ❌ Card grids for list inventories
- ❌ PageHeader title on list indexes (detail pages can keep headers)
- ❌ Line separators between list items
